  m_Name: PancitCantonDishReflection
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  dishName: Pancit Pusit
  dishSprite: {fileID: 0}
  pages:
  - 'Nice work. The platter in front of you is more than a meal. In Chinese and Filipino
    tradition, '
  - 'long noodles symbolise long life, and serving pancit at a birthday is a way
    of wishing the honouree many more years. '
  - "The two Chinese linguistic layers in the dish\u2019s name (Hokkien \u201Cpancit\u201D,
    Cantonese \u201Ccanton\u201D),"
  - ' record two separate currents of Chinese migration that met in Philippine panciterias
    and produced something new.'
  - Only Cavite City, with its unique colonial history, could have brought the three
    together in one dish.
  - When you keep the noodles long and uncut, you are honouring, a tradition that
    is older than most of the countries where this dish is now served.
